MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Logitech keyboard feels useful for more comfortable typing and touchpad control with my Raspberry Pi; it offers a practical improvement over my mini keyboard.",
    "The longer USB extensions fit my desk organization needs, while the memory card and reader could help me try Raspberry Pi images after checking compatibility. Both support activities already reflected in my purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another HDMI cable and more Ethernet leads repeat needs I have already addressed, without offering a length or use I currently need.",
    "The optical audio cable and Fire TV Stick assume a home entertainment project I have not shown interest in, while the 24-port switch and large internal SSDs assume expansion projects I do not currently have."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying cables seems to have been taken as a reason to suggest more cables, even when they would duplicate what I already have.",
    "My interest in computer accessories seems to have been stretched to include large storage upgrades, extensive networking equipment, and TV streaming devices without a clear connection to my current tasks."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Ethernet cables and adapter suggest I have already addressed basic wired connectivity; additional equipment needs a specific remaining purpose.",
    "What matters is how an accessory improves my existing setup: easier Raspberry Pi control, better peripheral placement, or removable storage for experiments. Capacity alone does not make an upgrade useful to me."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in practical computer accessories but often confused related equipment with something my current setup actually needs."
}
